  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Does there exist a pair of symplectic 4–manifolds $(X_{1}, \\omega_{1})and (X_{2}, \\omega_{2})$, where there is a diffeomorphism $f: X_{1} \\to X_{2}$ such that $f*(c_{1}(X_{2}, \\omega_{2})) = c_{1}(X_{1}, \\omega_{1})$ and $f*([\\omega_{2}]) = [\\omega_{1}] \\in H^{2}(X_{1},\\mathbb{R})$, but $(X_{1}, \\omega_{1})$ is not symplectomorphic to $(X_{2}, \\omega_{2})$?",
